{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MadronichColumn",
    "description": "The Madronich photolysis column, closed: optical depths and spherical geometry, the delta-Eddington two-stream solve, and the wavelength integral that turns the result into the 21 photolysis frequencies RADM2 reads (WRF-Chem phot_opt = 1, chem/module_phot_mad.F of WRF v4.8.0).\n\nThis is the document that answers the question the project started from. The instrumented dumps showed jv[52,59] arriving as an INPUT to the RADM2 KPP integrator, so RADM2 alone was not a column tendency. Here the j-values are computed from the column state instead, and checked against what WRF produced.\n\nTwo components are mounted and nothing about the radiation field is supplied: MadronichOpticalDepth builds the Rayleigh, ozone, aerosol and cloud optical depths per bin, applies the delta-Eddington scaling, runs sphers's pseudo-spherical slant-path geometry and produces the direct beam; MadronichTwoStream closes the 138-unknown tridiagonal two-stream system per wavelength bin and produces both diffuse streams. Only the cross sections and quantum yields arrive as data, and those are pinned on their own by MadronichSpectra.\n\nTHE SECOND, INDEPENDENT CHECK. The expected values are phot1_s from the photolysis dump. The instrumented fork established separately that ph_* = 60 phot1 and that WRF's generated KPP interface divides by 60 again, so phot1_s(n,k) IS jv(n,k) of the integrator -- measured at 1.1e-7 relative across four model times against dumps/radm2_wrf/*.json, which is a different dump written by a different subroutine. So these numbers are cross-checked against the chemistry's own input, not merely against the photolysis code's output.\n\nSCOPE: the clear column. subgrid inserts extra levels inside cloud, which makes the RT grid SIZE a function of the cloud field (70, 72, 77 and 78 at the four dumped daytime calls); a fixed-size index set cannot express that. Call 1410 is the one dumped daytime call whose column is completely cloud-free."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 69,
      "description": "Radiative-transfer layers, 69."
    },
    "NBIN": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 101,
      "description": "Active wavelength bins, 101."
    },
    "NJ": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 21,
      "description": "Photolysis channels RADM2 reads."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NLEV"
    },
    "lev_nodes": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "NLEV",
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "wlbin": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NBIN"
    },
    "jrate": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NJ"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Od": {
      "ref": "../components/gaschem/madronich/optical_depth.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV",
        "NBIN": "NBIN"
      }
    },
    "Ts": {
      "ref": "../components/gaschem/madronich/two_stream.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV",
        "NBIN": "NBIN"
      }
    },
    "MadronichColumn": {
      "variables": {
        "fldir_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes",
            "wlbin"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Coupling target: the direct-beam actinic flux from MadronichOpticalDepth."
        },
        "fldn_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes",
            "wlbin"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Coupling target: the down-welling diffuse actinic flux from MadronichTwoStream."
        },
        "flup_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes",
            "wlbin"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Coupling target: the up-welling diffuse actinic flux from MadronichTwoStream."
        },
        "sigma_qy": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "jrate",
            "wlbin"
          ],
          "units": "cm^2",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Cross section times quantum yield for each of RADM2's 21 photolysis channels at this level, in the order o31d, o33p, no2, no3o2, no3o, hno2, hno3, hno4, h2o2, ch2or, ch2om, ch3cho, ch3coch3, ch3coc2h5, hcocho, ch3cocho, hcochest, ch3o2h, ch3coo2h, ch3ono2, hcochob. Supplied from MadronichSpectra, which is pinned separately (36 assertions); carrying it as a parameter keeps this document to one level and therefore small."
        },
        "jlev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Which radiative-transfer level the j-values are evaluated at, 1 = the surface."
        },
        "actinic": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ],
          "units": "cm^-2 s^-1",
          "description": "Actinic flux per bin at that level, fext (fldir + fldn + flup) -- the sum of ALL THREE streams, which is the quantity photolysis acts on."
        },
        "j": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "jrate"
          ],
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "The 21 photolysis frequencies RADM2 reads, in s^-1. Equal to phot1_s, which is bit-for-bit jv(1:21) of the RADM2 KPP integrator."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
